From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: mm: do not flush the cache for slab folios

flush_dcache_folio() cleans and invalidates a whole slab folio on every
flush_dcache_page() of kmalloc memory; slab memory has no mapping and
is never mapped to user space, so skip it.
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/mm/flush.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/mm/flush.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mm/flush.c
@@ -350,6 +350,16 @@ void flush_dcache_folio(struct folio *fo
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Slab memory is not page cache and is not mapped to user space by
+	 * the kernel: only its linear mapping can hold dirty lines, and DMA
+	 * coherency is handled by the DMA API. Skip the clean of the whole
+	 * folio (32 KiB for kmalloc-4k) that flush_dcache_page() callers
+	 * such as memcpy_to_sglist() would trigger on every skb head.
+	 */
+	if (folio_test_slab(folio))
+		return;
+
 	mapping = folio_flush_mapping(folio);
 
 	if (!cache_ops_need_broadcast() &&
